# AI-Based Log Investigation Platform

An AI-driven cyber forensic platform designed to automate security log analysis across Windows, Linux, Network, and Web application environments. The system combines feature engineering, machine learning, explainable AI, and forensic reporting to help security analysts identify suspicious activity, prioritize investigations, and generate actionable evidence.

---

# Executive Summary

Security Operation Centers (SOCs) process enormous volumes of security events every day. Manual investigation of authentication logs, process execution events, network activity, and application logs is time-consuming and often leads to delayed incident response.

The AI-Based Log Investigation Platform was developed to automate large portions of this workflow using machine learning. The platform ingests logs from multiple sources, performs feature engineering, detects anomalous behavior using supervised and unsupervised learning models, explains predictions using SHAP/LIME, maps suspicious events to MITRE ATT&CK techniques, and generates structured forensic reports.

The project demonstrates the integration of data engineering, machine learning, cybersecurity, and explainable AI into a unified investigation pipeline.

---

# Problem Statement

Security analysts are frequently overwhelmed by the volume and diversity of security logs generated by enterprise environments.

Challenges include:

- Multiple heterogeneous log formats
- High false-positive rates
- Manual investigation of suspicious events
- Lack of explainability in AI-based detections
- Difficulty correlating events across multiple log sources

The objective of this project was to automate log investigation while maintaining transparency in AI-generated decisions.

---

# Motivation

This project was inspired by real-world Security Operations Center (SOC) workflows and Digital Forensics & Incident Response (DFIR) processes.

Primary goals included:

- Automating repetitive log analysis tasks
- Applying machine learning to cybersecurity datasets
- Improving analyst productivity
- Generating explainable security alerts
- Producing investigation-ready forensic evidence

